Maven 
=====
=> Maven is a build tool developed by Apache Organization 
=> Maven is developed using Java Language 
=> Maven is free software 
=> Maven is used to automate build process of the project

What Maven Can do ?

Maven creates project structure.
===============================
1) Download Required Dependencies 
2) Add dependencies to project build path .
3) Compile project source code.
4) Execute Unit test cases of project (Junits) .
5) Package our project as jar or war file
6) Maven creates project structure.
Current version of maven is as of now 3.9.11

Maven Terminology :
=================
=> Archetype: It represents type of project we want to create 
=> quickstart: standalone application webapp: web application 
=> groupId: It represents org name ex: com.tcs com.ibm.
=> artifactId : It represents project name ex: flipkart_app amazon_app 
=> version: It represents project version
=> SNAPSHOT: Under development
=> RELEASE: Develoment completed (production) 
=> Packaging: How you want to package your app (jar / war )
   quickstart: standalone application jar 
   webapp : web application ==> war file

